  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Development Goals County Dialogue &amp;  High-level Political Forum Support</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Agenda 2030 for Sustainable Development was adopted by UN Member States in September 2015. Included in the Agenda are 17 Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs) and 169 associated targets, described as &#x201c;integrated and indivisible, global in nature and universally applicable, taking into account different national realities, capacities and levels of development and respecting national policies and priorities.&#x201d; 
Through the Agenda Member States noted  commitment to and importance of SDG&apos;s in development. Caritas Kenya continues to  amplify voice of community and Church in addressing critical sustainability issues such as poverty, climate change, inequality, economic development, ecosystem protection and Agenda 2030 implementation processes. This grant is to facilitate CARITAS Kenya engagement at national, county and input into SDG&apos;s high political forum meeting July 2017</narrative>
  </description>
